      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Asset extraction — the index goes in, the contents do not",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-09-20:\n\n> *\"make sure you have zip ingestion skills to extract metadata of assets into\n> KG. don't extract contents unless explict ask by user.\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "library/skills/library-core/asset-extraction.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "What is NOT dropped silently",
      "prov:value": "They go in `omitted[]`\nwith a pattern, a reason and a count — measured on the IRIS zip: 11 real\nentries, 12 shadows."
    },
    {
      "@id": "library/skills/library-core/asset-extraction.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Derived renderings — the artefact we MADE, out of bytes we hold",
      "prov:value": "`pdf-cover.py` renders\npage 1 and calls it the cover, for the same reason `pdf-pages.py` sections by\npage: page 1 is a determined answer and \"the cover\" is not. Measured across\nthe three items, page 1 is the cover in all three and looks different in each\n— a portrait designed cover (2:3), a landscape one (0.705:1), and a scanned\ntitle page."
    },
    {
      "@id": "library/skills/library-core/asset-extraction.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Derived renderings — the artefact we MADE, out of bytes we hold",
      "prov:value": "A gate that re-renders a\nderived artefact needs the backend that produced it — and the CI job that runs\nthis repository's gates installs `ruff` and nothing else, which is stated on\n`ingest-stdlib`'s own Tool node and was walked into anyway: `iris:covers:check`\nthrew `pymupdf is not installed` on every run and turned a branch red three\ntimes."
    },
    {
      "@id": "library/skills/library-core/asset-extraction.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Related",
      "prov:value": "It moved down from the content core with the\n  script that writes it (bean `tlat`, placement PR5), because this skill is\n  the harness's own.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean tlat"
      ]
    }
